  "readout": "soft-clip length at each end of the best anchored SILVA alignment, on UNTRIMMED reads. A non-template prefix predicts a sharp mode at a fixed length on one mate's 5' end, absent from its own 3' end and from the other mate",
  "bias": "adapter read-through clips 3' ends and inflates the within-read control, which makes a real 5' excess harder to see, not easier. Divergence from the SILVA entry clips both ends and cancels in the difference. The DNA library is 0.01% ribosomal so its row is a statement about the reference, not the library",
